(*!
<summary>Beckhoff EL3403 phase channel with its own input status semantics.</summary>
<description>
Combines EL3403 phase feedback and the output variable-value selector.
Input Index acknowledges output Index; evaluate phase and terminal-wide diagnostics before using values.
Do not substitute POWER_MEASUREMENT_CHANNEL: its input status belongs to EL3413/EL3433.
Link input/output fields individually. Use one owner task and synchronize other access.
Copies store data only; they create no hardware links and do not guarantee an atomic snapshot.
When used for I/O, link located fields or their containing buffers to the matching selected PDOs.
The record is not a packed wire buffer; compiler padding is not part of the device specification.
Unlinked/default values do not prove valid I/O. The caller evaluates bus/channel validity before use.
Use one owner task per instance and externally synchronize other access; multi-field snapshots are not atomic.
Copies store data without creating hardware links. Keep borrowed field references valid while consumers are bound.
This passive record performs no validation, synchronization, configuration or protocol advancement.
</description>
*)
TYPE EL3403_CHANNEL :
STRUCT
	In : EL3403_INPUT_CHANNEL;
	Out : POWER_MEASUREMENT_OUTPUT_CHANNEL;
END_STRUCT
END_TYPE]]></Declaration>
  </DUT>
</TcPlcObject>
